  <section class="story-to-software wrap" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <h2 id="workflow-title">Give your agents a shared specification.</h2>
    <p>When requirements live in chat history, agents can lose context and reviewers have no shared definition of done. Solomonar keeps agreed behavior in version-controlled specifications, gives each task acceptance criteria, and separates implementation from review.</p>
    <p><strong>Spec-driven development</strong> means agreeing on what software should do before asking an agent to implement it, then checking the result against that specification. The framework connects <a href="{{ '/docs/framework/#the-book-specifications' | url }}">specifications</a>, <a href="{{ '/docs/framework/#the-spells-skills' | url }}">agent skills</a>, and <a href="{{ '/docs/framework/#the-reins-orchestration' | url }}">orchestration and review</a> in one workflow.</p>
    <p>The design targets Claude Code and Codex, with a language-agnostic core. Runtime adapter installation and project initialization are still in development. See the <a href="{{ '/docs/cli/' | url }}">current CLI commands</a> and <a href="{{ '/docs/use-cases/' | url }}">workflow examples with agent prompts</a>.</p>
